Now, Connie and I and our family were uh standing backstage and somebody walked up and I got to say, "Governor Acton."
刚才，康妮、我和家人站在后台，有人走过来，我就不得不喊她，“阿克顿州长！”

9
00:01:01,300 --> 00:01:06,580
I actually called her Governor Acton during all these rallies, one-on-one, because I knew she was going to win.
事实上，在这些集会私下见面时，我一直都叫她“阿克顿州长”，因为我知道她会赢。

10
00:01:06,580 --> 00:01:10,440
But still calling her Governor Acton after she speaks to all of you.
但在她刚刚向大家讲话之后，真的这样称呼她，感觉还是不同。

11
00:01:10,800 --> 00:01:11,180
Thank you.
谢谢。

12
00:01:11,180 --> 00:01:11,600
Thank you.
谢谢。

13
00:01:11,600 --> 00:01:12,080
Thank you.
谢谢。

14
00:01:17,540 --> 00:01:20,240
This is your victory.
这是你们的胜利。

15
00:01:23,510 --> 00:01:27,270
Corporations, billionaires tried to buy this election.
大公司、亿万富翁，曾试图买下这场选举。

16
00:01:28,050 --> 00:01:28,590
You know that.
你们都知道。

17
00:01:29,370 --> 00:01:44,390
But as it turns out, as it turns out, there are a whole lot more of us than there are of them.
但事实证明，我们的人数，远远多于他们。

18
00:01:44,400 --> 00:01:50,530
This campaign, this election are about you, the people who make our state and our country work.
这场竞选、这场选举，关乎你们，关乎让这个州和这个国家运转起来的人。

19
00:01:53,280 --> 00:02:01,260
Maybe maybe you put groceries back at the register when you see the total ticking up and up.
也许你在收银台看着总价不断上涨，只好把买好的食品放回去。

20
00:02:01,860 --> 00:02:11,420
Maybe your anxiety spikes as you drive up to the gas station wondering how much you are going to have to pay this week for gas.
也许你每次开进加油站，就焦虑起来，不知道这个星期又得花多少钱加油。

21
00:02:12,400 --> 00:02:17,100
You work hard every single day and you work.
你每天辛勤工作，一直工作。

22
00:02:18,080 --> 00:02:26,000
So often you feel like it's never enough to afford groceries, to afford health care and gas and utilities, Everything.
却常常觉得，无论如何都不够支付食品、医疗、汽油、水电，以及一切生活开支。

23
00:02:26,680 --> 00:02:35,580
Your work, your talent, your ingenuity, your determination, your work ethic power our state and fuel our country.
你们的劳动、才华、创造力、决心与勤劳，推动着这个州，支撑着整个国家。

24
00:02:40,670 --> 00:02:50,030
And the only reason that corporations are making billions and billions in profit, the only reason is because of you.
那些公司之所以能赚取数十亿、上百亿的利润，唯一的原因，就是你们。

25
00:02:53,060 --> 00:03:01,200
We've not had an economy and we've not had a government that works for you, that fights for you until now.
过去，我们没有一个真正为你们工作、为你们奋斗的经济体制与政府；但从现在起，不同了。

26
00:03:08,840 --> 00:03:12,540
You sent an undeniable message tonight.
今晚，你们发出了无法否认的信息。

27
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:15,360
Ohio is not for sale.
俄亥俄州，绝不出售。

28
00:03:20,310 --> 00:03:24,290
Ohio Ohio Ohio is not giving up on the dream of this country.
俄亥俄州没有放弃这个国家的梦想。

29
00:03:24,290 --> 00:03:28,350
That we're a place where anyone who works hard can get ahead.
那就是：只要努力工作，任何人都能够出人头地。

30
00:03:29,090 --> 00:03:31,610
That what matters is not your wealth.
真正重要的，不是财富。

31
00:03:31,610 --> 00:03:33,430
It is not your connections.
不是关系。

32
00:03:33,450 --> 00:03:34,690
It's not your last name.
不是你的姓氏。

33
00:03:34,770 --> 00:03:37,670
It's not the circumstances of your birth.
不是你的出身。

34
00:03:37,990 --> 00:03:39,070
It's your ingenuity.
而是你的创造力。

35
00:03:39,270 --> 00:03:39,910
It's your talent.
你的才华。

36
00:03:40,410 --> 00:03:41,010
It's your Yes.
是你的——没错。

37
00:03:41,210 --> 00:03:42,230
It's your work ethic.
是你勤恳工作的精神。

38
00:03:47,150 --> 00:04:00,789
Our our government should work for you, for Ohio, for the American people, not just the wealthy, not just the well-connected.
我们的政府，应该为你们、为俄亥俄、为美国人民工作，而不只是为富人和权贵。

39
00:04:00,789 --> 00:04:02,770
That is what we voted for today.
这就是我们今天投票所支持的东西。

40
00:04:05,820 --> 00:04:14,200
It's why It's why one of the first things I'm going to do in in the Senate is ban members of Congress from trading stocks.
因此，回到参议院后，我首先要做的事情之一，就是禁止国会议员交易股票。

41
00:04:20,160 --> 00:04:23,770
And you all know how corruption is woven into everything.
你们知道，腐败如何渗透到方方面面。

42
00:04:23,970 --> 00:04:26,030
Working people pay for this corruption.
而为腐败买单的，是劳动人民。

43
00:04:26,210 --> 00:04:30,270
Higher utility bills, higher grocery prices, higher drug prices.
更高的水电账单、更贵的食品、更高的药价。

44
00:04:30,910 --> 00:04:36,510
Starting today, Ohioans have a senator who puts working people first.
从今天起，俄亥俄人民拥有了一位将劳动者放在第一位的参议员。

45
00:04:43,660 --> 00:04:48,520
Ohioans voted for change because we all know the system is rigged.
俄亥俄人投票要求改变，因为大家都知道，这套体制被操纵了。

46
00:04:48,520 --> 00:04:56,040
And my pledge to all Ohioans, whether you voted for me or you didn't, is that I will always be on your side.
我向所有俄亥俄人承诺：无论你有没有投票给我，我都会始终站在你们这一边。

47
00:04:56,040 --> 00:04:56,580
Always.
始终如此。

48
00:05:02,020 --> 00:05:04,940
I do not work for the utility companies.
我不为公用事业公司工作。

49
00:05:07,820 --> 00:05:10,300
I do not work for data centers.
不为数据中心工作。

50
00:05:14,180 --> 00:05:16,120
I do not work for Wall Street.
不为华尔街工作。

51
00:05:19,080 --> 00:05:19,920
I work for you.
我为你们工作。

52
00:05:20,020 --> 00:05:20,860
I work for Ohio.
我为俄亥俄工作。

53
00:05:22,940 --> 00:05:25,860
So, we will fight to end these tariffs.
所以，我们将努力结束这些关税。

54
00:05:27,680 --> 00:05:31,640
We will end this war.
我们将结束这场战争。

55
00:05:37,110 --> 00:05:43,510
We will fight to lower your costs and increase your paychecks and open up paths to the middle class.
我们将努力降低你们的生活成本、提高你们的工资，为更多人打开通往中产阶层的道路。

56
00:05:48,120 --> 00:05:53,020
And as I have always done, I will take on anyone who stands in the way.
正如我一直所做的，我会挑战任何挡在前面的人。

57
00:05:56,290 --> 00:06:11,110
Because when you love this state, when you love this country, you fight for the people who make it work.
因为热爱这个州、热爱这个国家，就应该为那些让它运转的人奋斗。

58
00:06:21,860 --> 00:06:25,000
So, I want to take a few want to take a moment to thank a few people.
现在，我想花一点时间，感谢一些人。

59
00:06:25,258 --> 00:06:29,600
I mean, all of you I look through this crowd and I you showed up.
也就是你们所有人。我看着这满屋的人，你们来了。

60
00:06:30,120 --> 00:06:31,640
You all got off the sidelines.
你们走下了观望的看台。

61
00:06:31,800 --> 00:06:32,440
You showed up.
你们站了出来。

62
00:06:32,740 --> 00:06:33,700
You fought like hell.
你们全力以赴地奋战。

63
00:06:34,020 --> 00:06:35,220
You've made such a difference.
你们带来了如此巨大的改变。

64
00:06:35,560 --> 00:06:42,460
And you're the reason that Amy and I and so many that were were on the ticket this year have been successful.
艾米、我，以及今年名单上的许多候选人之所以成功，正是因为你们。

65
00:06:42,620 --> 00:06:43,200
So, thank you.
所以，谢谢你们。

66
00:06:46,180 --> 00:06:50,600
I want to thank the union staff at the Hilton serving us tonight.
我要感谢今晚在希尔顿酒店为我们服务的工会工作人员。

67
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:52,120
Thank you for the work you do.
谢谢你们所做的工作。

68
00:06:57,090 --> 00:07:02,130
I want to thank the law enforcement officers keeping us safe today and every day.
感谢今天，以及每一天守护我们安全的执法人员。

69
00:07:05,030 --> 00:07:08,213
Thank you for your sacrifices and for your public service.
谢谢你们的牺牲与公共服务。

70
00:07:09,010 --> 00:07:29,909
Now, let me talk about my family for a moment on stage with me, Connie Schultz.
现在说说我的家人。和我一起站在台上的，是康妮·舒尔茨。

71
00:07:29,909 --> 00:07:32,670
Wonderful, wonderful wife, wonderful mother.
一位出色的妻子，一位出色的母亲。

72
00:07:33,310 --> 00:07:48,020
Wonderful grandmother and oh yeah, one of the most talented and best writers in the nation Over the last two years,
一位出色的祖母；当然，也是全国最有才华、最优秀的作家之一。过去两年，

73
00:07:48,600 --> 00:07:55,720
And you have seen it, Connie inspired all of us pretty much every day with her fierce belief in hope.
你们都看到了，康妮几乎每天都用她对希望的坚定信念激励我们。

74
00:07:56,320 --> 00:08:02,360
Connie often quotes the author Nick Cave: an optimist with a broken heart.
她常引用作家尼克·凯夫的话：一个心碎了，却依然乐观的人。

75
00:08:03,840 --> 00:08:15,340
And that's um I you know go back a long time and go back a short time think about two years when all of us began this journey to to fix this
这让我想到过去，想到两年前，我们所有人一起踏上修复这个州的旅程，

76
00:08:15,340 --> 00:08:16,800
State and fix this country.
也修复这个国家。

77
00:08:17,280 --> 00:08:23,500
And there wasn't a lot of hope from a lot of people but there's a whole lot of hope from people I know in this crowd and from Connie.
那时，很多人没有多少希望；但我知道，这间屋子里有很多人，还有康妮，始终怀有巨大的希望。

78
00:08:23,720 --> 00:08:24,380
So thank you.
所以，谢谢。

79
00:08:29,360 --> 00:08:31,260
Our children and our grandchildren are here.
我们的孩子和孙辈们都在这里。

80
00:08:32,060 --> 00:08:34,440
And bear with me, there are a lot of them as you can see.
请容我多说一会儿，你们看，人确实不少。

81
00:08:35,720 --> 00:08:45,990
Um, Emily, Elizabeth, Caitlyn, Andy, Stina, Alejandro, Matt, Clayton, Leo, Jackie, Carolyn, Ella, Milo, Russell, Marbel.
埃米莉、伊丽莎白、凯特琳、安迪、斯蒂娜、亚历杭德罗、马特、克莱顿、利奥、杰姬、卡罗琳、埃拉、迈洛、拉塞尔、马贝尔。

82
00:08:45,990 --> 00:08:46,960
How lucky we are.
我们何其幸运。

83
00:08:51,140 --> 00:08:54,760
You know, I hate I'm going to acknowledge something.
我要承认一件事，虽然我不太想承认。

84
00:08:54,760 --> 00:09:02,740
And I shouldn't, but I have all the grandchildren's names on the teleprompter only because you just never know.
我本不该这样，但提词器上确实写着所有孙辈的名字，因为谁知道呢。

85
00:09:02,760 --> 00:09:03,380
I'm a little nervous.
我有一点紧张。

86
00:09:03,600 --> 00:09:05,100
I don't do this kind of speech very often.
毕竟，我不是经常发表这种讲话。

87
00:09:05,440 --> 00:09:09,080
If I left out one of them, you know the price that Connie and I would pay.
如果漏掉其中一个，你们知道，康妮和我会付出怎样的代价。

88
00:09:10,620 --> 00:09:11,920
So, right, Carol.
对吧，卡罗尔？

89
00:09:13,720 --> 00:09:18,150
Especially if it were Jackie or Carol.
尤其如果漏掉的是杰姬或卡罗尔。

90
00:09:18,190 --> 00:09:22,190
And I want to talk about our extended family all throughout this room.
我也想说说，今晚遍布这间屋子的另一个大家庭。

91
00:09:22,950 --> 00:09:27,690
All the staff on this campaign who gave everything to this cause and I mean everything.
这场竞选中为共同事业付出一切的工作人员；我说的是一切。

92
00:09:33,240 --> 00:09:42,900
The commitment they had, the hours they worked over the last two years and all of the staff who gave so much to the state for years before that.
过去两年他们的投入、他们工作的无数小时，以及在此前多年里同样为这个州倾尽心力的所有工作人员。

93
00:09:43,220 --> 00:09:44,600
So many of you are here tonight.
今晚，你们很多人都在这里。

94
00:09:45,060 --> 00:09:46,080
It says so much.
这本身就说明了很多。

95
00:09:46,180 --> 00:10:26,230
All the staff, come join us on stage.
所有工作人员，请一起上台来。

96
00:10:26,230 --> 00:10:36,280
And as they join us, it includes the some of them came uh were in my office before when I was in Washington or were the previous campaign.
正在走上来的这些人中，有些曾在我的华盛顿办公室工作，有些参与过过去的竞选。

97
00:10:36,280 --> 00:10:45,360
Uh many of them came from elsewhere now and so many of them traveled here tonight to be part of this for me to thank and for us to thank them.
还有很多人后来从其他地方加入；今晚，许多人特地赶来，让我、让我们有机会感谢他们。

98
00:10:45,780 --> 00:11:02,310
So keep on coming.
继续往上来。

99
00:11:08,720 --> 00:11:10,796
They're still coming.
他们还在上来。

100
00:11:14,990 --> 00:11:15,290
Sorry.
抱歉。

101
00:11:15,350 --> 00:11:16,690
I didn't know it was going to take this long.
我不知道要花这么久。

102
00:11:16,930 --> 00:11:17,130
Sorry.
抱歉。

103
00:11:18,750 --> 00:11:19,470
Everybody up.
大家都上来。

104
00:11:20,290 --> 00:11:29,217
Ann, come on.
安，来吧。

105
00:11:29,217 --> 00:11:53,086
Ann, I can move down.
安，我可以往下站一点。

106
00:11:53,086 --> 00:12:03,990
Just up.
上来就好。

107
00:12:04,080 --> 00:12:05,880
